        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "H.-O. Georgii, Large deviations and the equivalence of ensembles for Gibbsian particle systems with superstable interaction",
              "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/LDPsuperstable.pdf",
              "locator": "Theorems 1–2, printed pp.178–187 / PDF pp.8–17: energy density, free/periodic Gibbs variational formula, and pressure limit. The complete proofs in Sections 3–5 were read; local entropy and spatial-information inputs are separately supplied on the MP8 page."
            },
            {
              "title": "H.-O. Georgii and H. Zessin, Large deviations and the maximum entropy principle for marked point random fields",
              "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/GiiZess.pdf",
              "locator": "Sections 2.3, 3, and 5, printed pp.184–195 and 197–204 / complete 28-page PDF: Poisson-reference entropy, upper/lower empirical-field estimates, and conditional laws."
            },
            {
              "title": "D. Ruelle, Superstable Interactions in Classical Statistical Mechanics",
              "url": "https://www.ihes.fr/~ruelle/PUBLICATIONS/%5B28%5D.pdf",
              "locator": "Sections 1–2, printed pp.131–141 / PDF pp.4–14: superstability cell estimates and finite-volume interaction bounds."
            },
            {
              "title": "D. Dereudre, Introduction to the theory of Gibbs point processes",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1701.08105",
              "locator": "Sections 1.2–1.3, PDF pp.7–12: pair energy and finite-volume Poisson-Gibbs normalization; its infinite-volume variational theorem assumes finite range and is not used here."
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 6,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "proof": "**Given:** The assumptions and suppliers in Facts & Assumptions.\n\n1.1 Georgii's Theorem 1 [L1] gives existence of $\\Phi(P)$ and lower semicontinuity for every stationary finite-intensity law. Its Euclidean radial tail hypothesis follows from ours: $|x|_\\infty\\leq|x|_2\\leq\\sqrt d\\,|x|_\\infty$, so replacing $\\psi(r)$ by $\\psi(r/\\sqrt d)$ preserves monotonicity and finite weighted integral by a change of variables. The stable-plus-positive-core definition matches the source's superstable condition after choosing a smaller Euclidean core ball. Thus $\\Phi$ has exactly the domain and convention in the Statement. [F1, F2, L1, algebra]\n\n1.2 The cell estimate [F2] and $\\beta>0$ imply $J=I+\\beta\\Phi-\\rho\\log z$ is lower semicontinuous and coercive on bounded-$J$ sets: the Poisson entropy variational inequality with bounded truncations of $aN_{C_0}$ gives $I(P)\\geq a\\rho(P)-(e^a-1)$; the pointwise square inequality gives $E_PN_{C_0}^2\\geq\\rho(P)^2$. Hence bounded $J$ bounds $\\rho$, $I$, and $\\Phi$ from above. A finite candidate exists: take independent Bernoulli occupancy of widely separated small cubes, at most one absolutely continuously distributed point per cube, and a uniform random lattice phase. Each tile has finite relative entropy to Poisson, and the summable regular tail bounds its absolute intertile energy per volume. Thus $J$ is proper. By [F3] and the choice assumptions [A1], its bounded sublevels are compact in $\\tau_L$. [A1, F1, F2, F3, F7, F8, algebra]\n\n2.1 For the finite-volume Gibbs tilt $G_{L,z,\\beta,bc}$, direct integration gives $$ L^{-d}\\log Z_{L,z,\\beta,bc} =-L^{-d}D(G_{L,z,\\beta,bc}\\Vert Q_{\\Lambda_L}) -\\beta L^{-d}E_GH_{L,bc} +L^{-d}\\log z\\,E_GN. $$ Georgii's Theorem 2 [L2], applied with the present superstable regular interaction and $F=0$, supplies the matching upper and lower empirical-field bounds and the free/periodic pressure limit. Its upper proof uses this entropy identity, block stationarization, and the superstable cell cutoff; its lower proof conditions finite blocks on bounded finite-energy events, inserts empty corridors, and applies the spatial likelihood limit. The inspected source hypotheses match [F1]–[F8]: the Poisson reference is independent unit intensity, $\\tau_L$ is the local-tame topology [F5], entropy compactness is [F3], and the energy-density interface is [L1]. The theorem therefore yields $$ p_Q(z,\\beta)=-\\min_P\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\} $$ for both boundary conditions, with compact variational sublevels. [A1, F1, F3, F4, F5, F8, L1, L2, step 1.1]\n\n2.2 The minimum is attained: a minimizing sequence lies in a finite sublevel by the sparse finite candidate in step 1.2; compactness [F3] gives a convergent subsequence and lower semicontinuity from step 1.1 gives a minimizer. The set of minimizers is the closed minimum level within that compact sublevel, hence nonempty and compact. This agrees with the compact-sublevel conclusion in [L2]. [A1, F3, L2, step 1.2]\n\n3.1 The unit-intensity Poisson law on $\\Lambda_L$ has density $e^{-L^d}/N!$ relative to Lebesgue measure on the $N$-point sector. Therefore the physical partition $\\Xi_{L,z,\\beta}=e^{L^d}Z_{L,z,\\beta,\\mathrm{free}}$; its log rate is $p_Q+1$. This is only a positional normalization conversion. [F1, F6, L2, algebra] ∎\n",
        "library": "mathematics"
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-tdmath-van-hove-fixed-n-limit",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Exact canonical limit on arbitrary van Hove shapes",
        "statement": "Assume superstability and regularity, let $(\\Omega_k)$ be van Hove, and let $N_k/|\\Omega_k|\\to\\rho$ for an interior attainable density $\\rho>0$. Use the general-region free-wall convention of [[thm-tdmath-superstable-van-hove-pressure]], namely\n$$Z(\\Lambda,N;\\beta)=\\frac1{N!}\\int_{\\{q\\in\\Lambda^N:q_i\\neq q_j\\ (i\\neq j)\\}}\\exp\\!\\left(-\\beta\\sum_{1\\leq i<j\\leq N}\\phi(q_i-q_j)\\right)dq_1\\cdots dq_N\\quad(N\\geq1),$$\nwith $Z(\\Lambda,0;\\beta)=1$ and $e^{-\\beta(+\\infty)}=0$, for bounded Lebesgue-measurable $\\Lambda\\subset\\mathbb R^d$. For the free-wall exact-$N_k$ positional partition with this $1/N_k!$ normalization,\n$$|\\Omega_k|^{-1}\\log Z(\\Omega_k,N_k;\\beta)\\longrightarrow F_\\beta(\\rho),$$\nthe free-cube canonical rate of [[thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit]]. Superstability is used for the arbitrary-shape pressure upper bound; no stability-only upper theorem is asserted.",
        "deps": [
          "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction",
          "def-tdmath-van-hove-sequence",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality",
          "thm-tdmath-superstable-van-hove-pressure",
          "lem-tdmath-integrable-tail-diagonal-gap"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-tdmath-van-hove-sequence": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-superstable-van-hove-pressure": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-tdmath-integrable-tail-diagonal-gap": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "H.-O. Georgii, Large deviations and the equivalence of ensembles for Gibbsian particle systems with superstable interaction",
              "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/LDPsuperstable.pdf",
              "locator": "Sections 4 and 7, printed pp.181–195 / PDF pp.11–25: canonical density and shape boundary estimates."
            },
            {
              "title": "D. Ruelle, Superstable Interactions in Classical Statistical Mechanics",
              "url": "https://www.ihes.fr/~ruelle/PUBLICATIONS/%5B28%5D.pdf",
              "locator": "Sections 1–3, printed pp.131–145 / PDF pp.4–18: stability and summable interaction-tail estimates."
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 6,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "proof": "**Given:** The assumptions and suppliers in Facts & Assumptions.\n\n1.1 For any $\\alpha\\in\\mathbb R$, $e^{\\alpha N_k}Z(\\Omega_k,N_k)\\leq\\Xi_{\\Omega_k}(e^\\alpha,\\beta)$. Divide by volume, use [F5], and take the infimum over $\\alpha$. The duality [F4] gives $\\limsup |\\Omega_k|^{-1}\\log Z(\\Omega_k,N_k)\\leq F_\\beta(\\rho)$. [F4, F5, algebra]\n\n1.2 Choose $\\delta>0$ so $\\rho-\\delta,\\rho+\\delta$ lie in the attainable interior. For large core side $\\ell$, choose integers $n_-,n_+$ with $n_\\pm/\\ell^d\\to\\rho\\pm\\delta$. Put a central $\\ell$-cube inside each $(\\ell+g)$-cell, with $g=g(\\ell)$ from [F6]. The effective densities $n_\\pm/(\\ell+g)^d$ still bracket $\\rho$ when $\\ell$ is large. [F2, F3, F6, choose]\n\n2.1 At fixed $\\ell,g$, pack every complete $(\\ell+g)$-cell contained in $\\Omega_k$. Its count $M_k$ satisfies $M_k/|\\Omega_k|\\to(\\ell+g)^{-d}$ by [F2]. Assign $n_+$ particles to $j_k$ cores and $n_-$ to the remaining cores, except one correction core with remainder $r_k$ chosen to make the total exactly $N_k$. Bracketing ensures $0\\leq j_k<M_k$ for large $k$; Euclidean division gives $0\\leq r_k<n_+-n_- \\leq n_+$. Every correction integral $Z(\\ell,r)$, $0\\leq r\\leq n_+$, is positive: delete particles from a positive-measure finite-energy set realizing $Z(\\ell,n_+)>0$. There are finitely many such $r$, so the correction contributes $O_\\ell(1)$ to the log weight. [F1, F2, step 1.2, algebra]\n\n3.1 Exact assignment of labels cancels the global $N_k!$, leaving the product of core canonical integrals. The core lattice shell estimate bounds cross-energy per volume by $C K^2(\\ell/g)^d\\eta(g)$, where $K\\ell^d\\geq n_+$. Let $k\\to\\infty$ first, then $\\ell\\to\\infty$. The packing fraction tends one, the cross error tends zero, and the two rates tend $F_\\beta(\\rho-\\delta)$ and $F_\\beta(\\rho+\\delta)$. The bracketing proportions tend one half, so the lower rate is at least their average. Finally $\\delta\\downarrow0$; finite concavity makes $F_\\beta$ continuous at the interior density. Combined with step 1.1 this proves the limit. [F1, F2, F3, F6, step 2.1, algebra] ∎\n",
        "library": "mathematics"
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-tdmath-canonical-empirical-field-conditioning",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Conditioning grand empirical fields on an exact particle number",
        "statement": "Let $\\Lambda_L=[0,L)^d$, $\\beta,z>0$, and $b\\in\\{\\mathrm{free},\\mathrm{per}\\}$. On the simple labelled sector $\\mathcal S_{L,N}=\\{q\\in\\Lambda_L^N:q_i\\neq q_j\\ (i\\neq j)\\}$ use $H_{L,\\mathrm{free}}(q)=\\sum_{i<j}\\phi(q_i-q_j)$ and the periodic energy $H_{L,\\mathrm{per}}$ from [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]]. For $N\\geq1$ define\n$$Z_b(L,N;\\beta)=\\frac1{N!}\\int_{\\mathcal S_{L,N}}e^{-\\beta H_{L,b}(q)}\\,dq_1\\cdots dq_N,\\qquad Z_b(L,0;\\beta)=1,$$\nwith $e^{-\\beta(+\\infty)}=0$, and put $\\Xi_b(L,z,\\beta)=\\sum_{N\\geq0}z^NZ_b(L,N;\\beta)$. The unit-intensity Poisson reference $Q_{\\Lambda_L}$ has sector density $e^{-L^d}/N!$ relative to labelled Lebesgue measure, so its normalized grand partition is\n$$Z_{Q,b}(L;z,\\beta)=E_{Q_{\\Lambda_L}}[z^{N_{\\Lambda_L}}e^{-\\beta H_{L,b}}]=e^{-L^d}\\Xi_b(L,z,\\beta).$$\nThe exact-$N$ canonical law $C^b_{L,N}$ has density $e^{-\\beta H_{L,b}}/(N!Z_b(L,N;\\beta))$ on $\\mathcal S_{L,N}$, and the grand-canonical law $G^b_{L,z,\\beta}$ has density $z^{N_{\\Lambda_L}}e^{-\\beta H_{L,b}}/Z_{Q,b}(L;z,\\beta)$ relative to $Q_{\\Lambda_L}$. Let $\\rho>0$ be an interior attainable density, choose $\\alpha=\\log z$ supporting the free canonical rate $F_\\beta$ at $\\rho$, and take $N_L/L^d\\to\\rho$. Assume\n$$L^{-d}\\log Z_b(L,N_L;\\beta)\\longrightarrow F_\\beta(\\rho).$$\nLet $R_{L,\\omega}$ be the periodized empirical field of [[def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field]], and let\n$$\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}:=\\operatorname*{argmin}_{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}}\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\}.$$\nThen for every open $\\tau_L$ neighborhood $U$ of $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$ there is $c_U>0$ such that\n$$\\limsup_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log C^b_{L,N_L}\\{\\,\\omega:R_{L,\\omega}\\notin U\\,\\}\\leq-c_U.$$\nIf $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}=\\{P_*\\}$, then $R_{L,\\omega}\\to P_*$ in probability in $\\tau_L$ under $C^b_{L,N_L}$. This is a statement about spatially averaged local observables through the empirical field, not about the raw finite-box law at a fixed origin.",
        "deps": [
          "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction",
          "def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field",
          "lem-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field-stationary-density",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality",
          "thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field-stationary-density": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "dependency_level": 7,
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "H.-O. Georgii, Large deviations and the equivalence of ensembles for Gibbsian particle systems with superstable interaction",
              "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/LDPsuperstable.pdf",
              "locator": "Theorem 2 and Sections 3–5, printed pp.174–187 / PDF pp.4–17: good large-deviation principle for periodized empirical fields under free or periodic grand-canonical Gibbs laws; complete proof read."
            },
            {
              "title": "H.-O. Georgii and H. Zessin, Large deviations and the maximum entropy principle for marked point random fields",
              "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/GiiZess.pdf",
              "locator": "Sections 3 and 5: entropy upper bounds, empirical-field tightness, and conditional-law arguments."
            }
          ]
        },
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "proof": "**Given:** The hypotheses and suppliers in Facts & Assumptions.\n\n1.1 The canonical law is the grand law conditioned on $N=N_L$, since the grand weight on the $N_L$ sector differs from the canonical density only by the constant activity factor $z^{N_L}$. Its conditioning probability is $$G^b_{L,z,\\beta}(N=N_L)=\\frac{z^{N_L}e^{-L^d}Z_b(L,N_L;\\beta)}{Z_{Q,b}(L;z,\\beta)}.$$ Divide the logarithm by $L^d$. The numerator terms tend to $\\rho\\log z+F_\\beta(\\rho)-1$ by the assumed canonical rate and [F1]; the denominator tends to $p_Q(z,\\beta)$. By [F2]–[F3], $p_Q(z,\\beta)=F_\\beta(\\rho)+\\rho\\log z-1$, so $$L^{-d}\\log G^b_{L,z,\\beta}(N=N_L)\\longrightarrow0.$$ Thus the exact-number conditioning event has subexponential, positive grand probability for all sufficiently large $L$. [given, F1, F2, F3, algebra]\n\n1.2 Let $U$ be an open $\\tau_L$ neighborhood of $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$ and set $F=U^c$. The good rate in [L1] has zero set exactly $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$. Its infimum on the closed set $F$ is strictly positive: otherwise a sequence in $F$ with rates tending to zero would lie in a compact rate sublevel, have a limit in $F$, and by lower semicontinuity that limit would be a zero of the rate outside $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$. The large-deviation upper bound therefore gives some $c>0$ with $$\\limsup_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log G^b_{L,z,\\beta}\\{R_{L,\\omega}\\in F\\}\\leq-c.$$ [F3, F4, L1, algebra]\n\n2.1 Conditioning on $N=N_L$ yields $$C^b_{L,N_L}\\{R_{L,\\omega}\\notin U\\}\\leq \\frac{G^b_{L,z,\\beta}\\{R_{L,\\omega}\\in F\\}}{G^b_{L,z,\\beta}(N=N_L)}.$$ The numerator decays exponentially by step 1.2 and the denominator has zero exponential rate by step 1.1, so the ratio tends to zero. This proves concentration on every neighborhood of $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$. If the minimizer is unique, these neighborhood bounds are exactly convergence in probability in $\\tau_L$. [step 1.1, step 1.2, algebra] ∎\n",
        "library": "mathematics"
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-tdmath-fixed-n-local-ensemble-equivalence",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Fixed-particle local ensemble equivalence at interior density",
        "statement": "Assume the superstable regular model of [[thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure]], $\\beta>0$, and an interior attainable density $\\rho>0$. Let $N_L/L^d\\to\\rho$, let $C_{L,N_L}$ be the free-boundary positional canonical law with exactly $N_L$ particles, and let $R_{L,\\omega}$ be its periodized empirical field from [[def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field]]. Choose any finite supporting activity $z>0$ of $F_\\beta$ at $\\rho$ and set\n$$\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}:=\\operatorname*{argmin}_{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}}\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\}.$$\nFor every open $\\tau_L$ neighborhood $U$ of $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$,\n$$C_{L,N_L}\\{\\omega:R_{L,\\omega}\\in U\\}\\longrightarrow1.$$\nIf $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}=\\{P_*\\}$, then $R_{L,\\omega}\\to P_*$ in probability in $\\tau_L$. This is local observable equivalence for a uniformly sampled bulk location; it makes no claim about the raw finite-box law at a fixed origin or about uniqueness for every interaction.",
        "deps": [
          "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction",
          "def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field",
          "lem-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field-stationary-density",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality",
          "thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure",
          "lem-tdmath-canonical-empirical-field-conditioning"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field-stationary-density": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-interior-density-limit": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-canonical-grand-duality": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-tdmath-canonical-empirical-field-conditioning": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "H.-O. Georgii, Large deviations and the equivalence of ensembles for Gibbsian particle systems with superstable interaction",
              "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/LDPsuperstable.pdf",
              "locator": "Sections 3–5, printed pp.178–187 / PDF pp.8–17: stationary empirical fields, entropy bounds and variational minimizers."
            },
            {
              "title": "H.-O. Georgii and H. Zessin, Large deviations and the maximum entropy principle for marked point random fields",
              "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/GiiZess.pdf",
              "locator": "Sections 3 and 5: local entropy bounds and block stationarization."
            }
          ]
        },
        "dependency_level": 8,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "proof": "**Given:** The hypotheses and suppliers in Facts & Assumptions.\n\n1.1 Since $\\rho$ is interior and $F_\\beta$ is finite and concave there by [F1], it has a finite supporting slope $\\alpha$ at $\\rho$. Put $z=e^\\alpha>0$. [F1, algebra]\n\n2.1 The free exact-$N$ rate hypothesis of [F5] is exactly [F1], and [F2] supplies its supporting activity. The normalized/physical pressure conversion in [F3] is the equality required by [F5]; the empirical field is the stationary one in [F4]. Applying [F5] with free boundary gives concentration on $\\mathcal M_{z,\\beta}$ in every open $\\tau_L$ neighborhood. [F1, F2, F3, F4, F5, step 1.1]\n\n3.1 If the minimizer set is the singleton $\\{P_*\\}$, every open neighborhood of $P_*$ is a neighborhood of the full set. Step 2.1 therefore gives $C_{L,N_L}(R_{L,\\omega}\\notin U)\\to0$ for every open $U\\ni P_*$, which is convergence in probability in $\\tau_L$. [F5, step 2.1] ∎\n",
        "library": "mathematics"
      },
      {
        "id": "lem-tdmath-periodic-law-local-tame-transfer",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Periodic preparation and local-tame transfer from entropy bounds",
        "status": "draft",
        "origin": "pipeline",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "dependency_level": 5,
        "deps": [
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
