          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "H.-O. Georgii, Large deviations and the equivalence of ensembles for Gibbsian particle systems with superstable interaction",
              "url": "https://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~georgii/papers/LDPsuperstable.pdf",
              "locator": "Propositions 7.3–7.4, printed pp.193–194: translation-modulo-box invariance and entropy-controlled local convergence; the exact torus continuation and count-tail argument are developed here."
            }
          ]
        },
        "statement": "Assume AC, the ultrafilter extension principle, DC, and HB as in [[thm-tdmath-local-tame-entropy-compactness]]. Let $L\\to\\infty$ and let $C_L$ be probability laws on finite configurations in $\\Lambda_L=[0,L)^d$, invariant under every translation modulo $L\\mathbb Z^d$. Write $Q_L$ for unit-intensity Poisson measure and suppose\n$$c_L=L^{-d}D(C_L\\Vert Q_L),\\qquad \\sup_L c_L<\\infty.$$\nLet $\\widetilde C_L$ be the law of the periodic continuation. Then $\\widetilde C_L=E_{C_L}R_{L,\\omega}$; these laws are stationary and are relatively sequentially compact in $\\tau_L$ as $L\\to\\infty$. Their local counts are uniformly integrable. Along any convergent subsequence with limit $P$,\n$$I(P)\\leq\\liminf_L c_L.$$\nIf the empirical fields $R_{L,\\omega}$ converge in probability in $\\tau_L$ to a fixed $P_*$, then $\\widetilde C_L\\to P_*$ in $\\tau_L$, including expectations of every measurable local $f$ with $|f|\\leq b(1+N_A)$ for bounded $A$. This concerns periodic continuation, not the zero extension of a configuration outside its fundamental cube."
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-tdmath-retained-hard-zero-beta-limit",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Zero-inverse-temperature-parameter limit with forbidden pairs retained",
        "statement": "Let $\\phi$ be superstable and regular as in [[def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction]], and let $B=\\{x:\\phi(x)=+\\infty\\}$. For a finite configuration $\\omega$, call it admissible when no pair displacement belongs to $B$; for periodic boxes require this also for every periodic image pair. Define the zero-inverse-temperature-parameter continuation (the mathematical $\\beta=0$ branch) to be $z^{N(\\omega)}\\mathbf 1_{\\rm admissible}(\\omega)$, explicitly retaining the hard exclusion. Then the normalized Poisson free and periodic partition rates exist and equal\n$$-\\min_{P\\in\\mathcal K_B}\\{I(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\},$$\nwhere $\\mathcal K_B$ is the set of stationary laws with no forbidden pair almost surely. The minimizer set is nonempty and compact in $\\tau_L$. The periodically continued grand laws are relatively compact in $\\tau_L$, all their accumulation points are minimizers, and if this minimizer is unique they converge to it for every measurable local observable of at-most-linear count growth. If $B=\\varnothing$, this is the Poisson activity-$z$ model. For $B\\ne\\varnothing$, it is not an unrestricted Poisson law and does not assign a value to the undefined product $0\\cdot(+\\infty)$.",
        "deps": [
          "def-tdmath-superstable-regular-interaction",
