        "dependency_level": 7,
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "proof": "**Given:** The hypotheses and suppliers in Facts & Assumptions.\n\n1.1 Regularity bounds $\\phi$ above outside a bounded set, so $B$ is bounded. Define $\\chi=+\\infty$ on $B$ and $0$ elsewhere. Then $\\chi$ is even, stable with constant $0$, and has zero far tail. Its finite-volume beta-zero partition is exactly the specified hard-admissibility partition. [given, F1, algebra]\n\n1.2 For each bounded region $A$, the event that $A$ contains a forbidden pair is a bounded measurable local event. Its probability is continuous under $\\tau_L$ by [F6]. Exhausting space by countably many bounded cubes shows that $\\mathcal K_B$ is $\\tau_L$-closed. Apply [F4] to the bounded tests $f_M=a\\min(N_C,M)$ and let $M\\to\\infty$. Monotone convergence and [F7] give $I(P)\\geq a\\rho(P)-(e^a-1)$, hence $\\rho(P)\\leq(I(P)+e^a-1)/a$. Choosing $a>2\\max(\\log z,0)$ makes $I(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z$ coercive in $I(P)$. By [F2], every finite sublevel is compact and lower semicontinuous, so the infimum on $\\mathcal K_B$ is attained whenever the admissible class is nonempty. The empty configuration law gives a finite candidate. [F2, F4, F6, F7, algebra]\n\n1.3 Fix $P\\in\\mathcal K_B$ with $I(P)<\\infty$. Condition its restriction to a cube of side $n$ on configurations whose distinct points have separation at least $1/q$ and whose finite pair energies are at most $q$. As $q\\to\\infty$, these events increase to probability one because configurations are locally finite, simple, and hard-admissible. Choose $q=q(n)$ so the conditioning probability tends to one. Tile space by these conditioned blocks separated by an empty corridor wider than the range of $B$ and the fixed tail cutoff, take independent copies, then average the lattice phase uniformly. No cross-block pair is forbidden. The conditional entropy inequality $$ D(P(\\cdot\\mid E)\\Vert Q)\\leq [D(P\\Vert Q)+1]/P(E)-\\log P(E) $$ follows by expanding the conditional density $1_E(dP/dQ)/P(E)$ and using $-u\\log u\\leq1/e$. Additivity on independent blocks and the vanishing corridor fraction give $\\limsup I(P_n)\\leq I(P)$; local count truncation and finite first moments give $P_n\\to P$ in $\\tau_L$. Each $P_n$ has finite original energy density. [F1, F2, F4, F5, algebra]\n\n2.1 For a finite-volume beta-zero Gibbs law $G_L^b$, direct integration of its density gives $$ -\\log Z_{Q,L}=D(G_L^b\\Vert Q_L)-(\\log z)E_{G_L^b}N_L. $$ Stationarize independent blocks and average their phase. The entropy chain rule bounds the resulting specific entropy by the displayed finite-volume entropy per volume; hard admissibility passes to every local limit. Compactness [F2], lower semicontinuity, and the entropy identity therefore give the pressure upper bound by the negative minimum in the statement. For the reverse bound, use the approximating finite-energy laws from step 1.3. Their independent separated blocks are admissible; the spatial likelihood theorem [F3] supplies typical blocks with likelihood cost $I(P_n)$, while empirical counts converge to $\\rho(P_n)$. Changing from Poisson measure to the beta-zero weight gives the lower rate $-I(P_n)+\\rho(P_n)\\log z$. Let $n\\to\\infty$ and optimize over $P$. Corridors change the normalized log weight by their vanishing volume fraction, so free and periodic rates agree. [F2, F3, F5, step 1.3, algebra] ∎\n",
        "library": "mathematics"
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-tdmath-interval-event-ensemble-limit",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Interacting density-interval and upper-energy event limit",
        "statement": "Assume the superstable regular model and Poisson conventions of [[thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure]], with stationary finite-intensity law space $\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}$, intensity $\\rho$, specific entropy $I$, and energy density $\\Phi$ as there defined. Let $D\\subset[0,\\infty)$ be an interval of positive length and define\n$$\\nu=\\sup\\{\\rho(P):P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat},\\ I(P)<\\infty,\\ \\Phi(P)<\\infty\\},\\qquad e_0(\\rho)=\\inf\\{\\Phi(P):P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat},\\ \\rho(P)=\\rho,\\ I(P)<\\infty\\},$$\nwith the supremum of an empty set equal to $0$ and the infimum of an empty set equal to $+\\infty$. If $\\inf D<\\nu$ and $e>\\inf_{\\rho\\in D}e_0(\\rho)$, define\n$$A_L=\\{N_{\\Lambda_L}/L^d\\in D,\\ H_{L,\\mathrm{per}}/L^d\\leq e\\}.$$\nThen $A_L$ has positive Poisson probability for all sufficiently large $L$, and\n$$\\lim_{L\\to\\infty}L^{-d}\\log Q_{\\Lambda_L}(A_L) =-\\min\\{I(P):\\rho(P)\\in\\overline D,\\ \\Phi(P)\\leq e\\}.$$\nLet $R_{L,\\omega}$ be the periodized empirical field of [[def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field]], and let $B=\\{x\\in\\mathbb R^d:\\phi(x)=+\\infty\\}$. Define\n$$\\mathcal K_B=\\left\\{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}:P\\!\\left(\\left\\{\\omega:\\forall x,y\\in\\omega,\\ x\\neq y\\Rightarrow x-y\\notin B\\right\\}\\right)=1\\right\\}.$$\nFor $\\beta>0$ put $\\mathcal M_{\\beta,z}=\\operatorname*{argmin}_{P\\in\\mathcal P^1_{\\rm stat}}\\{I(P)+\\beta\\Phi(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\}$; at $\\beta=0$ put $\\mathcal M_{0,z}=\\operatorname*{argmin}_{P\\in\\mathcal K_B}\\{I(P)-\\rho(P)\\log z\\}$. Then there are $\\beta\\geq0$ and $z>0$ for which the empirical fields under the conditional law $Q_{\\Lambda_L}(\\cdot\\mid A_L)$ and the matching periodic grand-canonical law concentrate in every open $\\tau_L$ neighborhood of $\\mathcal M_{\\beta,z}$. If this minimizer set is a singleton, both empirical fields converge to it in probability in $\\tau_L$. These are empirical-field conclusions. The periodically continued conditional and grand laws also converge in $\\tau_L$ under the same uniqueness assumption, for all measurable local observables of at-most-linear count growth. The energy constraint is an upper event and $D$ is nondegenerate; this does not assert exact $N$, a shrinking shell, or a singular energy surface.\nIn the $\\beta=0$ branch the finite periodic weight is explicitly $z^N$ times the indicator that no displacement between the configuration and any periodic image lies in $B$; no value is assigned to $0\\cdot(+\\infty)$.",
        "deps": [
          "thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure",
          "lem-tdmath-closed-convex-separation",
          "thm-tdmath-specific-entropy-density",
          "lem-tdmath-relative-entropy-variational-and-chain-rules",
          "thm-tdmath-local-tame-entropy-compactness",
          "lem-tdmath-superstable-cell-energy-bound",
          "def-tdmath-local-tame-topology",
          "def-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field",
          "lem-tdmath-integrable-tail-diagonal-gap",
          "lem-tdmath-periodized-empirical-field-stationary-density",
          "lem-tdmath-periodic-law-local-tame-transfer",
          "thm-tdmath-retained-hard-zero-beta-limit"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "thm-tdmath-continuum-variational-pressure": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-tdmath-closed-convex-separation": "mathematical-premise",
